## Why This Is Asked
Tests a new, well-defined operator (Maj) within Kleene-like three-valued logic and requires concrete CSP reasoning with backtracking.

## Key Concepts
- Kleene three-valued logic semantics
- a custom 3-ary Maj operator (majority with T/F bias)
- constraint propagation and backtracking in non-binary domains

## Code Example
```javascript
function not(v){ return v==='T'?'F':v==='F'?'T':'U'; }
function maj(a,b,c){
  const t=[a,b,c].filter(x=>x==='T').length;
  const f=[a,b,c].filter(x=>x==='F').length;
  if(t>=2) return 'T';
  if(f>=2) return 'F';
  return 'U';
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you extend Maj to 4 inputs while preserving monotonicity?
- What is the impact of introducing additional unknowns on backtracking complexity?

## Why This Is Asked

To evaluate ability to design minimal-witness solvers for Horn-like rules and detect derivability with backtracking.

## Key Concepts

- Horn clauses
- Minimal witness extraction
- Forward-chaining with backtracking
- Cycle detection in derivations

## Code Example

```javascript
// simple forward-chaining for (A∧B)→C rules
function canDerive(target, base, rules){
  const derived = new Set(base);
  let changed = true;
  while (changed) {
    changed = false;
    for (const [A,B,C] of rules){
      if (derived.has(A) && derived.has(B) && !derived.has(C)){
        derived.add(C);
        changed = true;
      }
    }
  }
  return derived.has(target);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you extend to arbitrary antecedent sizes or negative literals?
- How would you enumerate all minimal witnesses or detect unsatisfiable cycles in large graphs?

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests reasoning with time-extended 3-valued logic and practical propagation strategies, not just static truth tables. It evaluates understanding of how constraints interact across temporal boundaries in non-classical logics.

## Key Concepts
- **Kleene 3-valued logic**: T > U > F, with ¬U = U, and A→B = ¬A ∨ B
- **Temporal propagation**: Constraints link time t0 to time t1, requiring forward reasoning
- **Forward checking with backtracking**: Propagate deterministically (F/T) first, defer U assignments for later exploration

## Code Example
```javascript
function propagateKleene(variables, constraints) {
  const domain = { T: 2, U: 1, F: 0 };

  function evalImplication(ant, cons) {
    if (ant === 'F') return 'T';
    if (ant === 'U') return 'U';
    return cons;
  }

  function forwardCheck() {
    let changed = true;
    while (changed) {
      changed = false;
      constraints.forEach(({antecedent, consequent, time}) => {
        const aVal = variables[antecedent + time];
        if (aVal === 'F') {
          if (variables[consequent + (time + 1)] === 'U') {
            variables[consequent + (time + 1)] = 'T';
            changed = true;
          }
        }
      });
    }
  }

  return { evalImplication, forwardCheck };
}
```
